## 2. OrcaPrinterAgent (template to copy)

`/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/Utils/OrcaPrinterAgent.hpp` and `.cpp` — full contents captured above. Key pattern: private members mirror every callback typedef (`OnMsgArrivedFn on_ssdp_msg_fn;` etc.), a `mutable std::mutex state_mutex;` guarding all setters/getters, every stub method just `return BAMBU_NETWORK_SUCCESS;` (or `true`/no-op), and a static `get_agent_info_static()` returning `AgentInfo{ORCA_PRINTER_AGENT_ID, "Orca", "0.0.1", "..."}` (id constants like `ORCA_PRINTER_AGENT_ID` live in `NetworkAgentFactory.hpp:17-18`). Constructor takes `std::string log_dir`.

## 3. Construction / registration site

Least invasive route: OrcaSlicer already has a **plugin registry**, not a compile-time switch. In `/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/Utils/NetworkAgentFactory.cpp`:

- Lines 132-154, `register_all_agents()`:
```cpp
void NetworkAgentFactory::register_all_agents()
{
    register_agent<OrcaPrinterAgent>();
    register_agent<QidiPrinterAgent>();
    register_agent<SnapmakerPrinterAgent>();
    register_agent<CrealityPrintAgent>();
    register_agent<MoonrakerPrinterAgent>();
    { /* BBLPrinterAgent registered manually, no log_dir ctor arg */ }
}
```
`register_agent<T>()` (lines 34-47) calls `T::get_agent_info_static()` for id/name and registers a factory lambda `make_shared<T>(log_dir)`. **To add `FakePrinterAgent` you only need one line: `register_agent<FakePrinterAgent>();`** inside `register_all_agents()`, plus `#include "FakePrinterAgent.hpp"` at the top — no other call site, no AppConfig flag, no compile switch needed. Selection is done at runtime via `NetworkAgentFactory::create_printer_agent_by_id(id, cloud_agent, log_dir)` (called when the user picks a printer, id stored in printer config's `host_type`/agent selector), and the UI populates choices from `get_registered_printer_agents()` — used in `/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/src/slic3r/GUI/PhysicalPrinterDialog.cpp:135` and `:159` (`auto agents = NetworkAgentFactory::get_registered_printer_agents();`) so a `FakePrinterAgent` with id `"fake"` would automatically show up in that picker too.

