## 5. Catch2 test infra

There is no `tests/agent/CMakeLists.txt` target for printer-agent tests specifically — `/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/tests/agent/CMakeLists.txt` builds a single executable `agent_bridge_tests` from a fixed file list (unrelated MCP/agent-bridge sources), linked against `Catch2WithMain`, `nlohmann_json`, `OpenSSL::Crypto`, `Boost::system`, `Threads::Threads`, and `jusprin_mcp_bridge_core`; registered via `orcaslicer_discover_tests(agent_bridge_tests)` at the bottom. To add a `FakePrinterAgent` test, either append a new `test_fake_printer_agent.cpp` to that same executable's source list (simplest, reuses existing link setup), or create a new `add_executable(...)` + `target_link_libraries(... Catch2WithMain ...)` + `orcaslicer_discover_tests(...)` block following that exact pattern in a sibling directory. Standard include is `<catch2/catch_all.hpp>` per `tests/CLAUDE.md`.
